+/* 컴파일러는 스레드마다 하나(설정이 호출마다 바뀌므로 공유 안 함) */
+static pthread_key_t ir_compiler_key;
+static pthread_once_t ir_key_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+static void
+ir_compiler_free(void *c) {
+  if (c && p_IRCompilerDestroy)
+    p_IRCompilerDestroy(c);
+}
+static void
+ir_make_key(void) {
+  pthread_key_create(&ir_compiler_key, ir_compiler_free);
+}
+static IRCompiler *
+ir_compiler(void) {
+  pthread_once(&ir_key_once, ir_make_key);
+  IRCompiler *c = pthread_getspecific(ir_compiler_key);
+  if (!c) {
+    c = p_IRCompilerCreate();
+    p_IRCompilerSetMinimumGPUFamily(c, IRGPUFamilyApple7);
+    p_IRCompilerSetMinimumDeploymentTarget(c, IROperatingSystem_macOS, "14.0.0");
+    p_IRCompilerSetStageInGenerationMode(c, IRStageInCodeGenerationModeUseMetalVertexFetch);
+    pthread_setspecific(ir_compiler_key, c);
+  }
+  return c;
+}
+
+static void
+fill_reflection(IRShaderReflection *refl, IRShaderStage stage, struct ember_dxil_reflection *out) {
+  out->stage = stage;
+  out->vertex_id_index = -1;
+  out->instance_id_index = -1;
+  if (stage == IRShaderStageVertex) {
+    IRVersionedVSInfo vs;
+    if (p_IRShaderReflectionCopyVertexInfo(refl, IRReflectionVersion_1_0, &vs)) {
+      out->needs_draw_params = vs.info_1_0.needs_draw_params;
+      out->vertex_id_index = vs.info_1_0.vertex_id_index;
+      out->instance_id_index = vs.info_1_0.instance_id_index;
+      out->vertex_output_size = vs.info_1_0.vertex_output_size_in_bytes;
+      size_t n = vs.info_1_0.num_vertex_inputs;
+      if (n > EMBER_DXIL_MAX_VS_INPUTS)
+        n = EMBER_DXIL_MAX_VS_INPUTS;
+      out->num_vs_inputs = (uint32_t)n;
+      for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) {
+        snprintf(out->vs_inputs[i].name, sizeof(out->vs_inputs[i].name), "%s",
+                 vs.info_1_0.vertex_inputs[i].name ? vs.info_1_0.vertex_inputs[i].name : "");
+        out->vs_inputs[i].attribute_index = vs.info_1_0.vertex_inputs[i].attributeIndex;
+      }
+      p_IRShaderReflectionReleaseVertexInfo(&vs);
+    }
+  } else if (stage == IRShaderStageFragment) {
+    IRVersionedFSInfo fs;
+    if (p_IRShaderReflectionCopyFragmentInfo(refl, IRReflectionVersion_1_0, &fs)) {
+      out->fs_num_render_targets = fs.info_1_0.num_render_targets;
+      out->fs_discards = fs.info_1_0.discards;
+      p_IRShaderReflectionReleaseFragmentInfo(&fs);
+    }
+  } else if (stage == IRShaderStageCompute) {
+    IRVersionedCSInfo cs;
+    if (p_IRShaderReflectionCopyComputeInfo(refl, IRReflectionVersion_1_0, &cs)) {
+      out->tg_size[0] = cs.info_1_0.tg_size[0];
+      out->tg_size[1] = cs.info_1_0.tg_size[1];
+      out->tg_size[2] = cs.info_1_0.tg_size[2];
+      p_IRShaderReflectionReleaseComputeInfo(&cs);
+    }
+  }
+}
+
+static int
+read_file(const char *path, void **data, size_t *size) {
+  FILE *f = fopen(path, "rb");
+  if (!f)
+    return 0;
+  fseek(f, 0, SEEK_END);
+  long n = ftell(f);
+  fseek(f, 0, SEEK_SET);
+  if (n <= 0) {
+    fclose(f);
+    return 0;
+  }
+  *data = malloc(n + 1);
+  *size = fread(*data, 1, n, f);
+  ((char *)*data)[*size] = 0;
+  fclose(f);
+  return *size == (size_t)n;
+}
+
+static void
+write_file_atomic(const char *path, const void *data, size_t size) {
+  char tmp[1100];
+  snprintf(tmp, sizeof(tmp), "%s.%d.tmp", path, (int)getpid());
+  FILE *f = fopen(tmp, "wb");
+  if (!f)
+    return;
+  size_t w = fwrite(data, 1, size, f);
+  fclose(f);
+  if (w == size)
+    rename(tmp, path);
+  else
+    unlink(tmp);
+}
+
+#define EMBER_DXIL_CACHE_VERSION "ember-dxil-4"
+
+/* Ember: 호환 플래그. 기본은 위치 불변·LOD 바이어스·최소 LOD·범위 검사(EMBER_DXIL_NOBOUNDS=1 이면 범위 검사 뺌).
+ * 시험용 EMBER_DXIL_COMPAT=<숫자> 는 통째로 바꾼다(IRCompatibilityFlags 비트, 캐시 키에 들어간다). */
+static uint32_t
+ember_compat_flags(void) {
+  const char *o = getenv("EMBER_DXIL_COMPAT");
+  if (o && *o)
+    return (uint32_t)strtoul(o, NULL, 0);
+  uint32_t compat = IRCompatibilityFlagPositionInvariance | IRCompatibilityFlagSamplerLODBias |
+                    IRCompatibilityFlagTextureMinLODClamp;
+  if (!getenv("EMBER_DXIL_NOBOUNDS"))
+    compat |= IRCompatibilityFlagBoundsCheck;
+  if (ir_v3)
+    compat |= (1u << 8); /* IRCompatibilityFlagForceTextureArray (3.0 헤더) */
+  return compat;
+}
+
+/* Ember: GS 반사만 얻는다(통과형인지, RT 배열 번호를 어느 VS 출력 레코드에서 받는지). 에뮬레이션 켜고 컴파일해야 GS 가 된다. */
+static NTSTATUS
+ember_gs_probe(struct unixcall_ember_dxil_compile *params, struct ember_dxil_reflection *out) {
+  out->gs_rt_array_index_record_id = -1;
+  out->gs_viewport_array_index_record_id = -1;
+  if (!p_IRShaderReflectionCopyGeometryInfo || !p_IRCompilerEnableGeometryAndTessellationEmulation) {
+    out->error_code = 0xffff;
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+  }
+  @autoreleasepool {
+    IRCompiler *c = ir_compiler();
+    IRError *err = NULL;
+    IRRootSignature *rs = NULL;
+    if (params->root_signature.ptr) {
+      rs = p_IRRootSignatureCreateFromDescriptor(params->root_signature.ptr, &err);
+      if (!rs) {
+        out->error_code = err ? p_IRErrorGetCode(err) : 0xfffe;
+        if (err)
+          p_IRErrorDestroy(err);
+        return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+      }
+    }
+    p_IRCompilerSetGlobalRootSignature(c, rs);
+    p_IRCompilerIgnoreRootSignature(c, rs != NULL);
+    if (ir_os_at_least_15())
+      p_IRCompilerSetMinimumDeploymentTarget(c, IROperatingSystem_macOS, "15.0.0");
+    p_IRCompilerEnableGeometryAndTessellationEmulation(c, true);
+    IRObject *input = p_IRObjectCreateFromDXIL(params->dxil.ptr, params->dxil_size, IRBytecodeOwnershipNone);
+    IRObject *output = input ? p_IRCompilerAllocCompileAndLink(c, NULL, input, &err) : NULL;
+    p_IRCompilerEnableGeometryAndTessellationEmulation(c, false);
+    p_IRCompilerSetMinimumDeploymentTarget(c, IROperatingSystem_macOS, "14.0.0");
+    p_IRCompilerSetGlobalRootSignature(c, NULL);
+    if (rs)
+      p_IRRootSignatureDestroy(rs);
+    if (!output) {
+      out->error_code = err ? p_IRErrorGetCode(err) : 0xfffd;
+      if (err)
+        p_IRErrorDestroy(err);
+      if (input)
+        p_IRObjectDestroy(input);
+      return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    }
+    IRShaderStage stage = p_IRObjectGetMetalIRShaderStage(output);
+    out->stage = stage;
+    IRShaderReflection *refl = p_IRShaderReflectionCreate();
+    if (p_IRObjectGetReflection(output, stage, refl)) {
+      IRVersionedGSInfo gi;
+      if (p_IRShaderReflectionCopyGeometryInfo(refl, IRReflectionVersion_1_0, &gi)) {
+        out->gs_is_passthrough = gi.info_1_0.is_passthrough;
+        out->gs_rt_array_index_record_id = gi.info_1_0.rt_array_index_record_id;
+        out->gs_viewport_array_index_record_id = gi.info_1_0.viewport_array_index_record_id;
+        out->gs_input_primitive = gi.info_1_0.input_primitive;
+        out->gs_instance_count = gi.info_1_0.instance_count;
+        out->gs_num_vertex_outputs = (uint32_t)gi.info_1_0.num_vertex_outputs;
+        if (ir_log)
+          fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil: GS probe passthrough=%d rt_id=%d vp_id=%d prim=%u instances=%u outputs=%zu\n",
+                  gi.info_1_0.is_passthrough, gi.info_1_0.rt_array_index_record_id,
+                  gi.info_1_0.viewport_array_index_record_id, gi.info_1_0.input_primitive, gi.info_1_0.instance_count,
+                  gi.info_1_0.num_vertex_outputs);
+        if (p_IRShaderReflectionReleaseGeometryInfo)
+          p_IRShaderReflectionReleaseGeometryInfo(&gi);
+      } else {
+        out->error_code = 0xfff9;
+      }
+    } else {
+      out->error_code = 0xfffc;
+    }
+    p_IRShaderReflectionDestroy(refl);
+    p_IRObjectDestroy(output);
+    p_IRObjectDestroy(input);
+  }
+  return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+NTSTATUS
+_EmberDXIL_compile(void *obj) {
+  struct unixcall_ember_dxil_compile *params = obj;
+  struct ember_dxil_reflection *out = params->reflection.ptr;
+  params->ret_function = 0;
+  pthread_once(&ir_once, ir_load);
+  if (!ir_ok) {
+    if (out) {
+      memset(out, 0, sizeof(*out));
+      out->error_code = 0xffff;
+      snprintf(out->error, sizeof(out->error), "libmetalirconverter.dylib not available");
+    }
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+  }
+  struct ember_dxil_reflection local;
+  if (!out)
+    out = &local;
+  memset(out, 0, sizeof(*out));
+  if (!params->dxil.ptr || !params->dxil_size) {
+    out->error_code = 0xfff0; /* 사용 가능 여부만 물어본 것 */
+    snprintf(out->error, sizeof(out->error), "no bytecode");
+    if ((params->flags & EMBER_DXIL_GS_PROBE) && p_IRCompilerSetVertexRenderTargetIndexID &&
+        p_IRShaderReflectionCopyGeometryInfo && p_IRCompilerEnableGeometryAndTessellationEmulation)
+      out->gs_is_passthrough = 0xabcd; /* 통과형 GS 제거를 할 수 있다는 표식 */
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+  }
+  if (params->flags & EMBER_DXIL_GS_PROBE)
+    return ember_gs_probe(params, out);
+  struct timespec t0, t1;
+  clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &t0);
+
+  @autoreleasepool {
+    const IRVersionedRootSignatureDescriptor *rsdesc = params->root_signature.ptr;
+
+    /* 캐시 키: 버전 + DXIL + 루트 시그니처(JSON) + 옵션 */
+    char key_hex[2 * CC_SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH + 1] = "";
+    const char *rs_json = NULL;
+    if (rsdesc)
+      rs_json = p_IRVersionedRootSignatureDescriptorCopyJSONString((IRVersionedRootSignatureDescriptor *)rsdesc);
+    if (ir_cache_dir[0]) {
+      CC_SHA256_CTX ctx;
+      CC_SHA256_Init(&ctx);
+      CC_SHA256_Update(&ctx, EMBER_DXIL_CACHE_VERSION, (CC_LONG)strlen(EMBER_DXIL_CACHE_VERSION));
+      CC_SHA256_Update(&ctx, ir_ident, (CC_LONG)strlen(ir_ident));
+#if defined(__x86_64__)
+      CC_SHA256_Update(&ctx, "x64", 3);
+#else
+      CC_SHA256_Update(&ctx, "a64", 3);
+#endif
+      CC_SHA256_Update(&ctx, params->dxil.ptr, (CC_LONG)params->dxil_size);
+      if (rs_json)
+        CC_SHA256_Update(&ctx, rs_json, (CC_LONG)strlen(rs_json));
+      uint32_t opts[3] = {params->int_rt_mask, params->flags, ember_compat_flags() ^ 0x1du}; /* 기본값이면 예전 키(0)와 같다 */
+      CC_SHA256_Update(&ctx, opts, sizeof(opts));
+      unsigned char md[CC_SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH];
+      CC_SHA256_Final(md, &ctx);
+      for (int i = 0; i < CC_SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH; i++)
+        sprintf(key_hex + 2 * i, "%02x", md[i]);
+    }
+
+    id<MTLDevice> device = (id<MTLDevice>)params->device;
+    void *lib_bytes = NULL;
+    size_t lib_size = 0;
+    IRShaderReflection *refl = NULL;
+    IRShaderStage stage = IRShaderStageInvalid;
+    char path_lib[1200] = "", path_json[1200] = "";
+
+    if (key_hex[0]) {
+      snprintf(path_lib, sizeof(path_lib), "%s/%.2s/%s.metallib", ir_cache_dir, key_hex, key_hex);
+      snprintf(path_json, sizeof(path_json), "%s/%.2s/%s.json", ir_cache_dir, key_hex, key_hex);
+      void *json = NULL;
+      size_t json_size = 0;
+      if (read_file(path_lib, &lib_bytes, &lib_size) && read_file(path_json, &json, &json_size)) {
+        /* 첫 줄: 스테이지 번호, 나머지: 반사 JSON */
+        char *nl = strchr((char *)json, '\n');
+        if (nl) {
+          stage = (IRShaderStage)atoi((char *)json);
+          refl = p_IRShaderReflectionCreateFromJSON(nl + 1);
+        }
+        out->from_cache = refl != NULL;
+      }
+      if (json)
+        free(json);
+      if (!refl && lib_bytes) {
+        free(lib_bytes);
+        lib_bytes = NULL;
+        lib_size = 0;
+      }
+    }
+
+    if (!refl) {
+      IRCompiler *compiler = ir_compiler();
+      IRError *err = NULL;
+      IRRootSignature *rs = NULL;
+      if (rsdesc) {
+        rs = p_IRRootSignatureCreateFromDescriptor(rsdesc, &err);
+        if (!rs) {
+          out->error_code = err ? p_IRErrorGetCode(err) : 0xfffe;
+          snprintf(out->error, sizeof(out->error), "root signature rejected (code %u)", out->error_code);
+          if (err)
+            p_IRErrorDestroy(err);
+          goto done;
+        }
+      }
+      p_IRCompilerSetGlobalRootSignature(compiler, rs);
+      p_IRCompilerIgnoreRootSignature(compiler, rs != NULL);
+      /* D3D 규칙에 맞춘다: 위치 불변(깊이 선패스 EQUAL), 샘플러 LOD 바이어스·최소 LOD(UE TAA 밉 바이어스), 범위 밖 읽기 = 0.
+       * 범위 검사는 비용이 있어 EMBER_DXIL_NOBOUNDS=1 로 끌 수 있다. 컴파일마다 다시 건다(일부 설정은 컴파일 뒤 풀린다). */
+      p_IRCompilerSetCompatibilityFlags(compiler, (IRCompatibilityFlags)ember_compat_flags());
+      p_IRCompilerSetIntRTMask(compiler, (uint8_t)params->int_rt_mask);
+      p_IRCompilerSetDualSourceBlendingConfiguration(
+          compiler, (params->flags & EMBER_DXIL_DUAL_SOURCE_BLEND) ? IRDualSourceBlendingConfigurationForceEnabled
+                                                                   : IRDualSourceBlendingConfigurationForceDisabled
+      );
+      /* Ember: 통과형 GS 를 없앤 VS — 지정한 출력 레코드를 [[render_target_array_index]]·[[viewport_array_index]] 로 */
+      int32_t rt_id = (int32_t)((params->flags >> 8) & 0xff) - 1, vp_id = (int32_t)((params->flags >> 16) & 0xff) - 1;
+      if (rt_id >= 0 && p_IRCompilerSetVertexRenderTargetIndexID)
+        p_IRCompilerSetVertexRenderTargetIndexID(compiler, rt_id);
+      if (vp_id >= 0 && p_IRCompilerSetVertexViewportIndexID)
+        p_IRCompilerSetVertexViewportIndexID(compiler, vp_id);
+      IRObject *input = p_IRObjectCreateFromDXIL(params->dxil.ptr, params->dxil_size, IRBytecodeOwnershipNone);
+      IRObject *output = input ? p_IRCompilerAllocCompileAndLink(compiler, NULL, input, &err) : NULL;
+      if (!output && input && err && p_IRErrorGetCode(err) == IRErrorCodeUnsupportedInstruction && ir_os_at_least_15()) {
+        /* Ember: globallycoherent UAV(UE4 의 계산 셰이더)는 macOS 15 대상에서만 된다. 기본 대상(14)은 캐시와
+         * 호환을 위해 그대로 두고, 이 오류일 때만 15 로 다시 컴파일한다. */
+        if (ir_log)
+          fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil: retry with macOS 15 target (%s)\n", ir_error_text(err));
+        p_IRErrorDestroy(err);
+        err = NULL;
+        p_IRCompilerSetMinimumDeploymentTarget(compiler, IROperatingSystem_macOS, "15.0.0");
+        output = p_IRCompilerAllocCompileAndLink(compiler, NULL, input, &err);
+        p_IRCompilerSetMinimumDeploymentTarget(compiler, IROperatingSystem_macOS, "14.0.0");
+      }
+      p_IRCompilerSetGlobalRootSignature(compiler, NULL);
+      if (rt_id >= 0 && p_IRCompilerSetVertexRenderTargetIndexID)
+        p_IRCompilerSetVertexRenderTargetIndexID(compiler, -1);
+      if (vp_id >= 0 && p_IRCompilerSetVertexViewportIndexID)
+        p_IRCompilerSetVertexViewportIndexID(compiler, -1);
+      if (rs)
+        p_IRRootSignatureDestroy(rs);
+      if (!output) {
+        out->error_code = err ? p_IRErrorGetCode(err) : 0xfffd;
+        snprintf(out->error, sizeof(out->error), "IRCompilerAllocCompileAndLink failed (code %u) %s", out->error_code,
+                 err ? ir_error_text(err) : "");
+        if (err)
+          p_IRErrorDestroy(err);
+        if (input)
+          p_IRObjectDestroy(input);
+        goto done;
+      }
+      stage = p_IRObjectGetMetalIRShaderStage(output);
+      IRMetalLibBinary *bin = p_IRMetalLibBinaryCreate();
+      if (p_IRObjectGetMetalLibBinary(output, stage, bin)) {
+        lib_size = p_IRMetalLibGetBytecodeSize(bin);
+        lib_bytes = malloc(lib_size);
+        p_IRMetalLibGetBytecode(bin, lib_bytes);
+      }
+      p_IRMetalLibBinaryDestroy(bin);
+      refl = p_IRShaderReflectionCreate();
+      if (!p_IRObjectGetReflection(output, stage, refl)) {
+        p_IRShaderReflectionDestroy(refl);
+        refl = NULL;
+      }
+      p_IRObjectDestroy(output);
+      p_IRObjectDestroy(input);
+      if (!lib_bytes || !refl) {
+        out->error_code = 0xfffc;
+        snprintf(out->error, sizeof(out->error), "no metallib/reflection for stage %d", (int)stage);
+        goto done;
+      }
+      if (path_lib[0]) {
+        const char *js = p_IRShaderReflectionCopyJSONString(refl);
+        if (js) {
+          char dir[1200];
+          snprintf(dir, sizeof(dir), "%s/%.2s", ir_cache_dir, key_hex);
+          mkdir(dir, 0755);
+          size_t jl = strlen(js);
+          char *buf = malloc(jl + 16);
+          int hl = snprintf(buf, 16, "%d\n", (int)stage);
+          memcpy(buf + hl, js, jl);
+          write_file_atomic(path_lib, lib_bytes, lib_size);
+          write_file_atomic(path_json, buf, hl + jl);
+          free(buf);
+          p_IRShaderReflectionReleaseString(js);
+        }
+      }
+    }
+
+    {
+      const char *entry = p_IRShaderReflectionGetEntryPointFunctionName(refl);
+      fill_reflection(refl, stage, out);
+      dispatch_data_t data =
+          dispatch_data_create(lib_bytes, lib_size, NULL, DISPATCH_DATA_DESTRUCTOR_DEFAULT); /* lib_bytes 소유권 넘김 */
+      lib_bytes = NULL;
+      NSError *nserr = nil;
+      id<MTLLibrary> lib = [device newLibraryWithData:data error:&nserr];
+      dispatch_release(data);
+      if (!lib) {
+        out->error_code = 0xfffb;
+        snprintf(out->error, sizeof(out->error), "newLibraryWithData: %s",
+                 nserr ? [[nserr localizedDescription] UTF8String] : "?");
+        goto done;
+      }
+      id<MTLFunction> fn = [lib newFunctionWithName:[NSString stringWithUTF8String:entry ? entry : "main"]];
+      if (!fn && [[lib functionNames] count])
+        fn = [lib newFunctionWithName:[[lib functionNames] objectAtIndex:0]];
+      [lib release];
+      if (!fn) {
+        out->error_code = 0xfffa;
+        snprintf(out->error, sizeof(out->error), "entry point %s not found", entry ? entry : "?");
+        goto done;
+      }
+      params->ret_function = (obj_handle_t)fn;
+    }
+
+  done:
+    if (lib_bytes)
+      free(lib_bytes);
+    if (refl)
+      p_IRShaderReflectionDestroy(refl);
+    if (rs_json)
+      p_IRVersionedRootSignatureDescriptorReleaseString(rs_json);
+  }
+
+  if (out->error_code && getenv("EMBER_DXIL_DUMP")) { /* 진단: 실패한 DXIL 을 떠 둔다 */
+    char path[1200];
+    snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s/fail-%u-%llx.dxil", getenv("EMBER_DXIL_DUMP"), out->error_code,
+             (unsigned long long)params->dxil_size ^ (unsigned long long)(uintptr_t)params->dxil.ptr);
+    write_file_atomic(path, params->dxil.ptr, params->dxil_size);
+  }
+  clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &t1);
+  out->compile_us = (uint32_t)((t1.tv_sec - t0.tv_sec) * 1000000 + (t1.tv_nsec - t0.tv_nsec) / 1000);
+  if (ir_log || out->error_code)
+    fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil: stage=%u %s %u us%s%s\n", out->stage, out->error_code ? "FAIL" : "ok",
+            out->compile_us, out->from_cache ? " (cache)" : "", out->error_code ? out->error : "");
+  if (ir_log && !out->error_code) {
+    if (out->stage == IRShaderStageCompute)
+      fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil:   tg=%u,%u,%u\n", out->tg_size[0], out->tg_size[1], out->tg_size[2]);
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < out->num_vs_inputs; i++)
+      fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil:   vs input '%s' -> attribute %u\n", out->vs_inputs[i].name, out->vs_inputs[i].attribute_index);
+    if (out->stage == IRShaderStageVertex)
+      fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil:   draw_params=%u vid=%d iid=%d\n", out->needs_draw_params, out->vertex_id_index, out->instance_id_index);
+  }
+  return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+/* ---- 정점 서술자: 같은 스레드의 다음 파이프라인 생성에 붙인다 ---- */
+
+static __thread MTLVertexDescriptor *pending_vd = nil;
+
+NTSTATUS
+_EmberMTL_setNextVertexDescriptor(void *obj) {
+  struct unixcall_ember_set_vertex_descriptor *params = obj;
+  if (pending_vd) {
+    [pending_vd release];
+    pending_vd = nil;
+  }
+  if (!params->num_attributes && !params->num_layouts)
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+  MTLVertexDescriptor *vd = [[MTLVertexDescriptor alloc] init];
+  const struct ember_vertex_attribute *a = params->attributes.ptr;
+  const struct ember_vertex_layout *l = params->layouts.ptr;
+  for (uint32_t i = 0; i < params->num_attributes; i++) {
+    if (a[i].attribute_index >= 31)
+      continue;
+    MTLVertexAttributeDescriptor *ad = vd.attributes[a[i].attribute_index];
+    ad.format = (MTLVertexFormat)a[i].format;
+    ad.offset = a[i].offset;
+    ad.bufferIndex = a[i].buffer_index;
+  }
+  for (uint32_t i = 0; i < params->num_layouts; i++) {
+    if (l[i].buffer_index >= 31)
+      continue;
+    MTLVertexBufferLayoutDescriptor *ld = vd.layouts[l[i].buffer_index];
+    ld.stride = MTLBufferLayoutStrideDynamic;
+    ld.stepFunction = (MTLVertexStepFunction)l[i].step_function;
+    ld.stepRate = l[i].step_function == MTLVertexStepFunctionConstant ? 0 : (l[i].step_rate ? l[i].step_rate : 1);
+  }
+  pending_vd = vd;
+  return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+/* _MTLDevice_newRenderPipelineState 가 부른다: 붙일 서술자가 있으면 넘기고 비운다 */
+MTLVertexDescriptor *
+ember_take_pending_vertex_descriptor(void) {
+  MTLVertexDescriptor *vd = pending_vd;
+  pending_vd = nil;
+  return vd; /* 부른 쪽이 release */
+}
+
+/* ---- Ember: 지오메트리 셰이더 에뮬레이션 파이프라인 (호출 156) ----
+ * Metal Shader Converter 의 방식(IRRuntimeNewGeometryEmulationPipeline 과 같은 조립):
+ *   VS -> 객체 함수 "<entry>.dxil_irconverter_object_shader" (tessellationEnabled=false), 정점 가져오기는 합성한
+ *         stage-in 함수를 객체 단계에 링크, GS -> 메시 함수(vertex_shader_output_size_fc = VS 출력 크기), PS -> 조각 함수.
+ * 캐시는 안 한다(GS 파이프라인은 게임마다 수십 개 정도). */
+
+MTLMeshRenderPipelineDescriptor *ember_new_mesh_descriptor(const struct WMTMeshRenderPipelineInfo *info);
+
+struct ember_ir_stage {
+  IRShaderStage stage;
+  void *lib_bytes;
+  size_t lib_size;
+  IRShaderReflection *refl;
+};
+
+static void
+ember_ir_stage_free(struct ember_ir_stage *st) {
+  if (st->lib_bytes)
+    free(st->lib_bytes);
+  if (st->refl)
+    p_IRShaderReflectionDestroy(st->refl);
+  memset(st, 0, sizeof(*st));
+}
+
+/* 이미 설정된 컴파일러로 하나 컴파일. 실패하면 0 과 err 문자열 */
+static int
+ember_ir_compile_one(IRCompiler *c, const void *dxil, size_t size, struct ember_ir_stage *st, char *err_out, size_t err_len,
+                     const char *what) {
+  memset(st, 0, sizeof(*st));
+  IRError *err = NULL;
+  IRObject *input = p_IRObjectCreateFromDXIL(dxil, size, IRBytecodeOwnershipNone);
+  IRObject *output = input ? p_IRCompilerAllocCompileAndLink(c, NULL, input, &err) : NULL;
+  if (!output) {
+    snprintf(err_out, err_len, "%s: compile failed (code %u) %s", what, err ? p_IRErrorGetCode(err) : 0xfffd,
+             err ? ir_error_text(err) : "");
+    if (err)
+      p_IRErrorDestroy(err);
+    if (input)
+      p_IRObjectDestroy(input);
+    return 0;
+  }
+  st->stage = p_IRObjectGetMetalIRShaderStage(output);
+  IRMetalLibBinary *bin = p_IRMetalLibBinaryCreate();
+  if (p_IRObjectGetMetalLibBinary(output, st->stage, bin)) {
+    st->lib_size = p_IRMetalLibGetBytecodeSize(bin);
+    st->lib_bytes = malloc(st->lib_size);
+    p_IRMetalLibGetBytecode(bin, st->lib_bytes);
+  }
+  p_IRMetalLibBinaryDestroy(bin);
+  st->refl = p_IRShaderReflectionCreate();
+  if (!p_IRObjectGetReflection(output, st->stage, st->refl)) {
+    p_IRShaderReflectionDestroy(st->refl);
+    st->refl = NULL;
+  }
+  p_IRObjectDestroy(output);
+  p_IRObjectDestroy(input);
+  if (!st->lib_bytes || !st->refl) {
+    snprintf(err_out, err_len, "%s: no metallib/reflection (stage %d)", what, (int)st->stage);
+    ember_ir_stage_free(st);
+    return 0;
+  }
+  return 1;
+}
+
+static id<MTLLibrary>
+ember_ir_library(id<MTLDevice> device, const void *bytes, size_t size, char *err_out, size_t err_len, const char *what) {
+  void *copy = malloc(size);
+  memcpy(copy, bytes, size);
+  dispatch_data_t data = dispatch_data_create(copy, size, NULL, DISPATCH_DATA_DESTRUCTOR_FREE);
+  NSError *nserr = nil;
+  id<MTLLibrary> lib = [device newLibraryWithData:data error:&nserr];
+  dispatch_release(data);
+  if (!lib)
+    snprintf(err_out, err_len, "%s: newLibraryWithData: %s", what, nserr ? [[nserr localizedDescription] UTF8String] : "?");
+  return lib;
+}
+
+static const char *
+ember_binding_type(MTLBindingType t) {
+  switch (t) {
+  case MTLBindingTypeBuffer: return "buffer";
+  case MTLBindingTypeThreadgroupMemory: return "tgmem";
+  case MTLBindingTypeTexture: return "texture";
+  case MTLBindingTypeSampler: return "sampler";
+  case MTLBindingTypeObjectPayload: return "payload";
+  default: return "other";
+  }
+}
+
+NTSTATUS
+_EmberDXIL_newGeometryPipeline(void *obj) {
+  struct unixcall_ember_gs_pipeline *call = obj;
+  struct ember_dxil_gs_pipeline *p = call->desc.ptr;
+  p->ret_pso = 0;
+  p->error_code = 0;
+  p->error[0] = 0;
+  p->vertex_buffer_table_index = 6;
+  pthread_once(&ir_once, ir_load);
+  if (!ir_ok || !p_IRCompilerEnableGeometryAndTessellationEmulation || !p_IRMetalLibSynthesizeStageInFunction ||
+      !p_IRShaderReflectionCopyGeometryInfo) {
+    p->error_code = 0xffff;
+    snprintf(p->error, sizeof(p->error), "geometry emulation not available in libmetalirconverter");
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+  }
+  struct timespec t0, t1;
+  clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &t0);
+
+  const char *dump = getenv("EMBER_DXIL_DUMP_GS"); /* 진단: GS 파이프라인 셰이더를 떠 둔다 */
+  if (dump) {
+    static int seq = 0;
+    int n = __sync_fetch_and_add(&seq, 1);
+    char path[1200];
+    snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s/gs%03d-vs.dxil", dump, n);
+    write_file_atomic(path, p->vs.ptr, p->vs_size);
+    snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s/gs%03d-gs.dxil", dump, n);
+    write_file_atomic(path, p->gs.ptr, p->gs_size);
+    if (p->ps.ptr) {
+      snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s/gs%03d-ps.dxil", dump, n);
+      write_file_atomic(path, p->ps.ptr, p->ps_size);
+    }
+  }
+
+  @autoreleasepool {
+    id<MTLDevice> device = (id<MTLDevice>)p->device;
+    IRCompiler *c = ir_compiler();
+    IRError *err = NULL;
+    IRRootSignature *rs = NULL;
+    struct ember_ir_stage vs = {0}, gs = {0}, ps = {0};
+    IRMetalLibBinary *stagein_bin = NULL;
+    id<MTLLibrary> vs_lib = nil, gs_lib = nil, ps_lib = nil, si_lib = nil;
+    id<MTLFunction> obj_fn = nil, mesh_fn = nil, frag_fn = nil, si_fn = nil;
+    MTLMeshRenderPipelineDescriptor *desc = nil;
+    uint32_t vs_out_size = 0;
+
+    if (p->root_signature.ptr) {
+      rs = p_IRRootSignatureCreateFromDescriptor(p->root_signature.ptr, &err);
+      if (!rs) {
+        p->error_code = err ? p_IRErrorGetCode(err) : 0xfffe;
+        snprintf(p->error, sizeof(p->error), "root signature rejected (code %u)", p->error_code);
+        if (err)
+          p_IRErrorDestroy(err);
+        goto done;
+      }
+    }
+    p_IRCompilerSetGlobalRootSignature(c, rs);
+    p_IRCompilerIgnoreRootSignature(c, rs != NULL);
+    p_IRCompilerSetCompatibilityFlags(c, (IRCompatibilityFlags)ember_compat_flags());
+    if (ir_os_at_least_15())
+      p_IRCompilerSetMinimumDeploymentTarget(c, IROperatingSystem_macOS, "15.0.0");
+    p_IRCompilerSetIntRTMask(c, 0);
+    p_IRCompilerSetDualSourceBlendingConfiguration(c, IRDualSourceBlendingConfigurationForceDisabled);
+    p_IRCompilerEnableGeometryAndTessellationEmulation(c, true);
+
+    /* VS: stage-in 은 따로 합성한다 */
+    p_IRCompilerSetStageInGenerationMode(c, IRStageInCodeGenerationModeUseSeparateStageInFunction);
+    int ok = ember_ir_compile_one(c, p->vs.ptr, p->vs_size, &vs, p->error, sizeof(p->error), "VS");
+    if (ok) {
+      stagein_bin = p_IRMetalLibBinaryCreate();
+      if (!p_IRMetalLibSynthesizeStageInFunction(c, vs.refl, p->input_layout.ptr, stagein_bin)) {
+        snprintf(p->error, sizeof(p->error), "stage-in synthesis failed");
+        ok = 0;
+      }
+    }
+    p_IRCompilerSetStageInGenerationMode(c, IRStageInCodeGenerationModeUseMetalVertexFetch);
+    if (ok)
+      ok = ember_ir_compile_one(c, p->gs.ptr, p->gs_size, &gs, p->error, sizeof(p->error), "GS");
+    p_IRCompilerEnableGeometryAndTessellationEmulation(c, false);
+    if (ok && p->ps.ptr) {
+      p_IRCompilerSetIntRTMask(c, (uint8_t)p->int_rt_mask);
+      p_IRCompilerSetDualSourceBlendingConfiguration(
+          c, (p->flags & EMBER_DXIL_DUAL_SOURCE_BLEND) ? IRDualSourceBlendingConfigurationForceEnabled
+                                                        : IRDualSourceBlendingConfigurationForceDisabled
+      );
+      ok = ember_ir_compile_one(c, p->ps.ptr, p->ps_size, &ps, p->error, sizeof(p->error), "PS");
+    }
+    p_IRCompilerSetMinimumDeploymentTarget(c, IROperatingSystem_macOS, "14.0.0");
+    p_IRCompilerSetGlobalRootSignature(c, NULL);
+    if (!ok) {
+      p->error_code = 0xfffd;
+      goto done;
+    }
+
+    {
+      IRVersionedVSInfo vi;
+      if (p_IRShaderReflectionCopyVertexInfo(vs.refl, IRReflectionVersion_1_0, &vi)) {
+        vs_out_size = vi.info_1_0.vertex_output_size_in_bytes;
+        p->vs_needs_draw_params = vi.info_1_0.needs_draw_params;
+        p_IRShaderReflectionReleaseVertexInfo(&vi);
+      }
+      IRVersionedGSInfo gi;
+      if (p_IRShaderReflectionCopyGeometryInfo(gs.refl, IRReflectionVersion_1_0, &gi)) {
+        p->gs_max_input_prims = gi.info_1_0.max_input_primitives_per_mesh_threadgroup;
+        p->gs_input_primitive = gi.info_1_0.input_primitive;
+        p->gs_instance_count = gi.info_1_0.instance_count;
+        if (ir_log)
+          fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil: GS passthrough=%d input_prim=%u max_prims/tg=%u payload=%u instances=%u vs_out=%u\n",
+                  gi.info_1_0.is_passthrough, gi.info_1_0.input_primitive,
+                  gi.info_1_0.max_input_primitives_per_mesh_threadgroup, gi.info_1_0.max_payload_size_in_bytes,
+                  gi.info_1_0.instance_count, vs_out_size);
+        if (p_IRShaderReflectionReleaseGeometryInfo)
+          p_IRShaderReflectionReleaseGeometryInfo(&gi);
+      }
+      p->gs_vertex_size = vs_out_size;
+      if (!p->gs_max_input_prims || !vs_out_size) {
+        p->error_code = 0xfff9;
+        snprintf(p->error, sizeof(p->error), "bad GS reflection (max prims %u, vs out %u)", p->gs_max_input_prims,
+                 vs_out_size);
+        goto done;
+      }
+    }
+
+    vs_lib = ember_ir_library(device, vs.lib_bytes, vs.lib_size, p->error, sizeof(p->error), "VS");
+    gs_lib = vs_lib ? ember_ir_library(device, gs.lib_bytes, gs.lib_size, p->error, sizeof(p->error), "GS") : nil;
+    if (gs_lib && ps.lib_bytes)
+      ps_lib = ember_ir_library(device, ps.lib_bytes, ps.lib_size, p->error, sizeof(p->error), "PS");
+    if (gs_lib) {
+      size_t n = p_IRMetalLibGetBytecodeSize(stagein_bin);
+      void *b = malloc(n);
+      p_IRMetalLibGetBytecode(stagein_bin, b);
+      si_lib = ember_ir_library(device, b, n, p->error, sizeof(p->error), "stage-in");
+      free(b);
+    }
+    if (!vs_lib || !gs_lib || !si_lib || (ps.lib_bytes && !ps_lib)) {
+      p->error_code = 0xfffb;
+      goto done;
+    }
+
+    {
+      MTLFunctionConstantValues *fc = [[MTLFunctionConstantValues alloc] init];
+      BOOL tess = NO;
+      [fc setConstantValue:&tess type:MTLDataTypeBool withName:@"tessellationEnabled"];
+      int32_t vsz = (int32_t)vs_out_size;
+      NSError *e = nil;
+      const char *ve = p_IRShaderReflectionGetEntryPointFunctionName(vs.refl);
+      NSString *oname = [NSString stringWithFormat:@"%s.dxil_irconverter_object_shader", ve ? ve : "main"];
+      obj_fn = [vs_lib newFunctionWithName:oname constantValues:fc error:&e];
+      if (!obj_fn) {
+        snprintf(p->error, sizeof(p->error), "object function %s: %s", [oname UTF8String],
+                 e ? [[e localizedDescription] UTF8String] : "?");
+        [fc release];
+        p->error_code = 0xfffa;
+        goto done;
+      }
+      [fc setConstantValue:&vsz type:MTLDataTypeInt withName:@"vertex_shader_output_size_fc"];
+      const char *ge = p_IRShaderReflectionGetEntryPointFunctionName(gs.refl);
+      e = nil;
+      mesh_fn = [gs_lib newFunctionWithName:[NSString stringWithUTF8String:ge ? ge : "main"] constantValues:fc error:&e];
+      [fc release];
+      if (!mesh_fn) {
+        snprintf(p->error, sizeof(p->error), "mesh function %s: %s", ge ? ge : "?",
+                 e ? [[e localizedDescription] UTF8String] : "?");
+        p->error_code = 0xfffa;
+        goto done;
+      }
+      if (ps_lib) {
+        const char *pe = p_IRShaderReflectionGetEntryPointFunctionName(ps.refl);
+        frag_fn = [ps_lib newFunctionWithName:[NSString stringWithUTF8String:pe ? pe : "main"]];
+        if (!frag_fn && [[ps_lib functionNames] count])
+          frag_fn = [ps_lib newFunctionWithName:[[ps_lib functionNames] objectAtIndex:0]];
+        if (!frag_fn) {
+          snprintf(p->error, sizeof(p->error), "fragment entry %s not found", pe ? pe : "?");
+          p->error_code = 0xfffa;
+          goto done;
+        }
+      }
+      if ([[si_lib functionNames] count])
+        si_fn = [si_lib newFunctionWithName:[[si_lib functionNames] objectAtIndex:0]];
+      if (!si_fn) {
+        snprintf(p->error, sizeof(p->error), "stage-in function missing");
+        p->error_code = 0xfffa;
+        goto done;
+      }
+    }
+
+    desc = ember_new_mesh_descriptor(p->mesh_info.ptr);
+    desc.objectFunction = obj_fn;
+    desc.meshFunction = mesh_fn;
+    desc.fragmentFunction = frag_fn;
+    {
+      MTLLinkedFunctions *lf = [[MTLLinkedFunctions alloc] init];
+      lf.functions = @[ si_fn ];
+      desc.objectLinkedFunctions = lf;
+      [lf release];
+    }
+    {
+      NSError *e = nil;
+      MTLAutoreleasedRenderPipelineReflection refl = nil;
+      MTLPipelineOption opt = MTLPipelineOptionBindingInfo;
+      id<MTLRenderPipelineState> pso = [device newRenderPipelineStateWithMeshDescriptor:desc
+                                                                                 options:opt
+                                                                              reflection:&refl
+                                                                                   error:&e];
+      if (!pso) {
+        p->error_code = 0xfff8;
+        snprintf(p->error, sizeof(p->error), "mesh pipeline: %s", e ? [[e localizedDescription] UTF8String] : "?");
+        goto done;
+      }
+      /* 객체 단계에서 정점 버퍼 표(IRRuntimeVertexBuffers)를 어디서 읽는지 반사로 찾는다. 실측 이름 "vertex_buffers_ab"
+       * (kIRVertexBufferBindPoint = 6). 못 찾으면 6 */
+      for (id<MTLBinding> b in refl.objectBindings) {
+        if (ir_log)
+          fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil:   object binding %s index=%lu type=%s\n", [b.name UTF8String],
+                  (unsigned long)b.index, ember_binding_type(b.type));
+        if (b.type == MTLBindingTypeBuffer && [b.name containsString:@"vertex_buffers"])
+          p->vertex_buffer_table_index = (uint32_t)b.index;
+      }
+      if (ir_log) {
+        for (id<MTLBinding> b in refl.meshBindings)
+          fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil:   mesh binding %s index=%lu type=%s\n", [b.name UTF8String],
+                  (unsigned long)b.index, ember_binding_type(b.type));
+        for (id<MTLBinding> b in refl.fragmentBindings)
+          fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil:   fragment binding %s index=%lu type=%s\n", [b.name UTF8String],
+                  (unsigned long)b.index, ember_binding_type(b.type));
+      }
+      p->ret_pso = (obj_handle_t)pso;
+    }
+
+  done:
+    ember_ir_stage_free(&vs);
+    ember_ir_stage_free(&gs);
+    ember_ir_stage_free(&ps);
+    if (stagein_bin)
+      p_IRMetalLibBinaryDestroy(stagein_bin);
+    if (rs)
+      p_IRRootSignatureDestroy(rs);
+    [vs_lib release];
+    [gs_lib release];
+    [ps_lib release];
+    [si_lib release];
+    [obj_fn release];
+    [mesh_fn release];
+    [frag_fn release];
+    [si_fn release];
+    [desc release];
+  }
+  clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &t1);
+  unsigned us = (unsigned)((t1.tv_sec - t0.tv_sec) * 1000000 + (t1.tv_nsec - t0.tv_nsec) / 1000);
+  if (ir_log || !p->ret_pso)
+    fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil: GS pipeline %s %u us %s (vbtable=%u)\n", p->ret_pso ? "ok" : "FAIL", us, p->error,
+            p->vertex_buffer_table_index);
+  return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+
+/* ---- Ember(d12games4): VS 의 stage-in 을 따로 합성 (호출 159) ----
+ * Metal 정점 가져오기(MTLVertexDescriptor)가 못 읽는 입력 형식(R10G10B10A2_UINT 등)을 쓰는 PSO 용. VS 를
+ * IRStageInCodeGenerationModeUseSeparateStageInFunction 으로 컴파일하고, D3D12 입력 배치로 stage-in 함수를 합성해(형식 변환은
+ * 셰이더 코드가 한다) 같은 스레드의 다음 _MTLDevice_newRenderPipelineState 에 vertexLinkedFunctions 로 붙인다.
+ * 정점 버퍼는 IRRuntimeVertexBuffers 표(kIRVertexBufferBindPoint = 6)로 읽는다. 캐시는 안 한다(이런 PSO 만 이 길로 온다). */
+
+static __thread id<MTLFunction> pending_stagein = nil;
+
+/* _MTLDevice_newRenderPipelineState 가 부른다: 붙일 stage-in 함수가 있으면 넘기고 비운다(부른 쪽이 release) */
+id<MTLFunction>
+ember_take_pending_stagein(void) {
+  id<MTLFunction> f = pending_stagein;
+  pending_stagein = nil;
+  return f;
+}
+
+NTSTATUS
+_EmberDXIL_compileStageIn(void *obj) {
+  struct unixcall_ember_dxil_stagein *call = obj;
+  struct ember_dxil_stagein *p = call->desc.ptr;
+  struct ember_dxil_reflection local, *out = p->reflection.ptr ? p->reflection.ptr : &local;
+  memset(out, 0, sizeof(*out));
+  p->ret_function = 0;
+  p->vertex_buffer_table_index = 6;
+  if (pending_stagein) {
+    [pending_stagein release];
+    pending_stagein = nil;
+  }
+  pthread_once(&ir_once, ir_load);
+  if (!ir_ok || !p_IRMetalLibSynthesizeStageInFunction) {
+    out->error_code = 0xffff;
+    snprintf(out->error, sizeof(out->error), "stage-in synthesis not available");
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+  }
+  struct timespec t0, t1;
+  clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &t0);
+  @autoreleasepool {
+    id<MTLDevice> device = (id<MTLDevice>)p->device;
+    IRCompiler *c = ir_compiler();
+    IRError *err = NULL;
+    IRRootSignature *rs = NULL;
+    struct ember_ir_stage vs = {0};
+    IRMetalLibBinary *si_bin = NULL;
+    id<MTLLibrary> vs_lib = nil, si_lib = nil;
+    id<MTLFunction> vs_fn = nil, si_fn = nil;
+    if (p->root_signature.ptr) {
+      rs = p_IRRootSignatureCreateFromDescriptor(p->root_signature.ptr, &err);
+      if (!rs) {
+        out->error_code = err ? p_IRErrorGetCode(err) : 0xfffe;
+        snprintf(out->error, sizeof(out->error), "root signature rejected (code %u)", out->error_code);
+        if (err)
+          p_IRErrorDestroy(err);
+        goto done;
+      }
+    }
+    p_IRCompilerSetGlobalRootSignature(c, rs);
+    p_IRCompilerIgnoreRootSignature(c, rs != NULL);
+    p_IRCompilerSetCompatibilityFlags(c, (IRCompatibilityFlags)ember_compat_flags());
+    p_IRCompilerSetIntRTMask(c, 0);
+    p_IRCompilerSetDualSourceBlendingConfiguration(c, IRDualSourceBlendingConfigurationForceDisabled);
+    int32_t rt_id = (int32_t)((p->flags >> 8) & 0xff) - 1, vp_id = (int32_t)((p->flags >> 16) & 0xff) - 1;
+    if (rt_id >= 0 && p_IRCompilerSetVertexRenderTargetIndexID)
+      p_IRCompilerSetVertexRenderTargetIndexID(c, rt_id);
+    if (vp_id >= 0 && p_IRCompilerSetVertexViewportIndexID)
+      p_IRCompilerSetVertexViewportIndexID(c, vp_id);
+    p_IRCompilerSetStageInGenerationMode(c, IRStageInCodeGenerationModeUseSeparateStageInFunction);
+    int ok = ember_ir_compile_one(c, p->vs.ptr, p->vs_size, &vs, out->error, sizeof(out->error), "VS");
+    if (!ok && ir_os_at_least_15()) {
+      p_IRCompilerSetMinimumDeploymentTarget(c, IROperatingSystem_macOS, "15.0.0");
+      ok = ember_ir_compile_one(c, p->vs.ptr, p->vs_size, &vs, out->error, sizeof(out->error), "VS");
+      p_IRCompilerSetMinimumDeploymentTarget(c, IROperatingSystem_macOS, "14.0.0");
+    }
+    if (ok) {
+      si_bin = p_IRMetalLibBinaryCreate();
+      if (!p_IRMetalLibSynthesizeStageInFunction(c, vs.refl, p->input_layout.ptr, si_bin)) {
+        snprintf(out->error, sizeof(out->error), "stage-in synthesis failed");
+        ok = 0;
+      }
+    }
+    p_IRCompilerSetStageInGenerationMode(c, IRStageInCodeGenerationModeUseMetalVertexFetch);
+    if (rt_id >= 0 && p_IRCompilerSetVertexRenderTargetIndexID)
+      p_IRCompilerSetVertexRenderTargetIndexID(c, -1);
+    if (vp_id >= 0 && p_IRCompilerSetVertexViewportIndexID)
+      p_IRCompilerSetVertexViewportIndexID(c, -1);
+    p_IRCompilerSetGlobalRootSignature(c, NULL);
+    if (!ok) {
+      out->error_code = 0xfffd;
+      goto done;
+    }
+    fill_reflection(vs.refl, vs.stage, out);
+    vs_lib = ember_ir_library(device, vs.lib_bytes, vs.lib_size, out->error, sizeof(out->error), "VS");
+    if (vs_lib) {
+      size_t n = p_IRMetalLibGetBytecodeSize(si_bin);
+      void *b = malloc(n);
+      p_IRMetalLibGetBytecode(si_bin, b);
+      si_lib = ember_ir_library(device, b, n, out->error, sizeof(out->error), "stage-in");
+      free(b);
+    }
+    if (!vs_lib || !si_lib) {
+      out->error_code = 0xfffb;
+      goto done;
+    }
+    {
+      const char *ve = p_IRShaderReflectionGetEntryPointFunctionName(vs.refl);
+      vs_fn = [vs_lib newFunctionWithName:[NSString stringWithUTF8String:ve ? ve : "main"]];
+      if (!vs_fn && [[vs_lib functionNames] count])
+        vs_fn = [vs_lib newFunctionWithName:[[vs_lib functionNames] objectAtIndex:0]];
+      if ([[si_lib functionNames] count])
+        si_fn = [si_lib newFunctionWithName:[[si_lib functionNames] objectAtIndex:0]];
+      if (!vs_fn || !si_fn) {
+        out->error_code = 0xfffa;
+        snprintf(out->error, sizeof(out->error), "%s function missing", vs_fn ? "stage-in" : "vertex");
+        goto done;
+      }
+    }
+    pending_stagein = si_fn; /* 넘김 */
+    si_fn = nil;
+    p->ret_function = (obj_handle_t)vs_fn;
+    vs_fn = nil;
+
+  done:
+    ember_ir_stage_free(&vs);
+    if (si_bin)
+      p_IRMetalLibBinaryDestroy(si_bin);
+    if (rs)
+      p_IRRootSignatureDestroy(rs);
+    [vs_lib release];
+    [si_lib release];
+    [vs_fn release];
+    [si_fn release];
+  }
+  clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &t1);
+  out->compile_us = (uint32_t)((t1.tv_sec - t0.tv_sec) * 1000000 + (t1.tv_nsec - t0.tv_nsec) / 1000);
+  if (ir_log || !p->ret_function)
+    fprintf(stderr, "ember-dxil: VS stage-in %s %u us %s\n", p->ret_function ? "ok" : "FAIL", out->compile_us, out->error);
+  return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
diff --git a/src/winemetal/unix/ember_fg_unix.c b/src/winemetal/unix/ember_fg_unix.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..56bbcb3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/winemetal/unix/ember_fg_unix.c
@@ -0,0 +1,551 @@
+/*
+ * Ember FG hook: unix side. Loads the optional libEmberFG.dylib (EmberCore, separate proprietary library, not part of
+ * this tree) from the directory of winemetal.so and forwards EmberFG_call operations to it. When the library is missing
+ * or has an incompatible ABI major version every call reports 0 and DXMT runs without frame generation.
+ * Integration: winemetal_unix.c appends &_EmberFG_call to both call tables at index EMBER_FG_UNIX_CALL (157).
+ *
+ * This library is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU Lesser
+ * General Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation; either version 2.1 of the License, or
+ * (at your option) any later version.
+ */
+#include <dlfcn.h>
+#include <pthread.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+#define WINEMETAL_API
+#include "../winemetal_thunks.h"
+#include "../ember_fg_thunks.h"
+
+typedef int NTSTATUS;
+#define STATUS_SUCCESS 0
+
+#define EMBER_FG_EXPECT_MAJOR 1
+
+static struct {
+  uint32_t (*abi_version)(void);
+  void *(*create)(uint64_t device, const char *env, size_t len);
+  void (*destroy)(void *ctx);
+  void (*get_config)(void *ctx, void *out);
+  int (*begin_frame)(void *ctx, const void *in, void *out);
+  int (*encode)(void *ctx, const void *in, void *out);
+  int (*ring_acquire)(void *ctx, const void *in, void *out);
+  void (*ring_release)(void *ctx, int32_t slot, int32_t frame_done);
+  void (*ring_wait_idle)(void *ctx);
+  void (*note_drop)(void *ctx, uint32_t kind);
+  void (*get_stats)(void *ctx, int64_t now, void *out);
+  size_t (*hud_text)(void *ctx, int64_t now, double fps, uint64_t generated, char *buf, size_t cap);
+  size_t (*drain_log)(void *ctx, char *buf, size_t cap);
+} fg;
+static uint32_t fg_version;
+static pthread_once_t fg_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+
+static void
+fg_load(void) {
+  char path[4096];
+  const char *override = getenv("EMBER_FG_LIB");
+  void *lib = NULL;
+  if (override && *override) {
+    snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s", override);
+  } else {
+    Dl_info info;
+    path[0] = 0;
+    if (dladdr((const void *)&fg_load, &info) && info.dli_fname) {
+      const char *slash = strrchr(info.dli_fname, '/');
+      if (slash) snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%.*s/libEmberFG.dylib", (int)(slash - info.dli_fname), info.dli_fname);
+    }
+  }
+  if (path[0]) lib = dlopen(path, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL);
+  if (!lib) return;
+#define SYM(field, name) *(void **)&fg.field = dlsym(lib, name)
+  SYM(abi_version, "ember_fg_abi_version");
+  SYM(create, "ember_fg_create");
+  SYM(destroy, "ember_fg_destroy");
+  SYM(get_config, "ember_fg_get_config");
+  SYM(begin_frame, "ember_fg_begin_frame");
+  SYM(encode, "ember_fg_encode");
+  SYM(ring_acquire, "ember_fg_ring_acquire");
+  SYM(ring_release, "ember_fg_ring_release");
+  SYM(ring_wait_idle, "ember_fg_ring_wait_idle");
+  SYM(note_drop, "ember_fg_note_drop");
+  SYM(get_stats, "ember_fg_get_stats");
+  SYM(hud_text, "ember_fg_hud_text");
+  SYM(drain_log, "ember_fg_drain_log");
+#undef SYM
+  if (!fg.abi_version || (fg.abi_version() >> 16) != EMBER_FG_EXPECT_MAJOR || !fg.create || !fg.destroy || !fg.get_config ||
+      !fg.begin_frame || !fg.encode || !fg.ring_acquire || !fg.ring_release || !fg.ring_wait_idle || !fg.note_drop ||
+      !fg.get_stats || !fg.hud_text || !fg.drain_log) {
+    memset(&fg, 0, sizeof(fg));
+    dlclose(lib);
+    return;
+  }
+  fg_version = fg.abi_version();
+}
+
+/* Ember in-game HUD: libEmberHUD.dylib (EmberCore, separate proprietary library) from the same directory. Optional — when it
+ * is missing the HUD ops report 0 and the Ember app keeps its separate overlay window. */
+static struct {
+  uint32_t (*abi_version)(void);
+  void *(*create)(uint64_t device, const char *env, size_t len, uint32_t host);
+  void (*destroy)(void *ctx);
+  int (*encode)(void *ctx, const void *in, void *out);
+} hud;
+static pthread_once_t hud_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+
+static void
+hud_load(void) {
+  char path[4096];
+  const char *override = getenv("EMBER_HUD_LIB");
+  void *lib = NULL;
+  Dl_info info;
+  path[0] = 0;
+  if (override && *override) snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s", override);
+  else if (dladdr((const void *)&hud_load, &info) && info.dli_fname) {
+    const char *slash = strrchr(info.dli_fname, '/');
+    if (slash) snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%.*s/libEmberHUD.dylib", (int)(slash - info.dli_fname), info.dli_fname);
+  }
+  if (path[0]) lib = dlopen(path, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL);
+  if (!lib) return;
+  *(void **)&hud.abi_version = dlsym(lib, "ember_hud_abi_version");
+  *(void **)&hud.create = dlsym(lib, "ember_hud_create");
+  *(void **)&hud.destroy = dlsym(lib, "ember_hud_destroy");
+  *(void **)&hud.encode = dlsym(lib, "ember_hud_encode");
+  if (!hud.abi_version || (hud.abi_version() >> 16) != 1 || !hud.create || !hud.destroy || !hud.encode) {
+    memset(&hud, 0, sizeof(hud));
+    dlclose(lib);
+  }
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS
+hud_call(struct unixcall_ember_fg *p) {
+  void *ctx = (void *)(uintptr_t)p->ctx;
+  pthread_once(&hud_once, hud_load);
+  if (!hud.encode) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+  switch (p->op) {
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_HUD_CREATE:
+    ctx = hud.create(p->device, (const char *)p->in.ptr, (size_t)p->in_size, 0 /* EMBER_HUD_HOST_DXMT */);
+    p->ctx = (obj_handle_t)(uintptr_t)ctx;
+    p->ret = ctx != NULL;
+    break;
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_HUD_ENCODE:
+    if (ctx) p->ret = hud.encode(ctx, p->in.ptr, p->out.ptr);
+    break;
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_HUD_DESTROY:
+    if (ctx) hud.destroy(ctx);
+    p->ret = 1;
+    break;
+  }
+  return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+/* Ember Tone / Ember Flare: libEmberTone.dylib (EmberCore, separate proprietary library) from the same directory
+ * (override EMBER_TONE_LIB). Optional — when it is missing the Tone ops report 0 and DXMT presents frames unchanged.
+ * ember_neural_unix.m (old unix calls 146..152) uses the same library through ember_tone_lib(). */
+static struct {
+  uint32_t (*abi_version)(void);
+  void *(*neural_create)(uint64_t device, const char *env, size_t len, uint32_t host);
+  void (*neural_destroy)(void *ctx);
+  int (*neural_encode)(void *ctx, const void *in, void *out);
+  void *(*ahdr_create)(uint64_t device, const char *env, size_t len, uint32_t host);
+  void (*ahdr_destroy)(void *ctx);
+  void (*ahdr_get_config)(void *ctx, void *cfg);
+  int (*ahdr_encode)(void *ctx, const void *in, void *out);
+  void (*ahdr_frame)(void *ctx, const void *in, void *out);
+  size_t (*drain_log)(void *ctx, char *buf, size_t cap);
+} tone;
+static void *tone_handle;
+static pthread_once_t tone_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+
+static void
+tone_load(void) {
+  char path[4096];
+  const char *override = getenv("EMBER_TONE_LIB");
+  void *lib = NULL;
+  Dl_info info;
+  path[0] = 0;
+  if (override && *override) snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s", override);
+  else if (dladdr((const void *)&tone_load, &info) && info.dli_fname) {
+    const char *slash = strrchr(info.dli_fname, '/');
+    if (slash) snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%.*s/libEmberTone.dylib", (int)(slash - info.dli_fname), info.dli_fname);
+  }
+  if (path[0]) lib = dlopen(path, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL);
+  if (!lib) return;
+#define TSYM(field, name) *(void **)&tone.field = dlsym(lib, name)
+  TSYM(abi_version, "ember_tone_abi_version");
+  TSYM(neural_create, "ember_tone_neural_create");
+  TSYM(neural_destroy, "ember_tone_neural_destroy");
+  TSYM(neural_encode, "ember_tone_neural_encode");
+  TSYM(ahdr_create, "ember_tone_ahdr_create");
+  TSYM(ahdr_destroy, "ember_tone_ahdr_destroy");
+  TSYM(ahdr_get_config, "ember_tone_ahdr_get_config");
+  TSYM(ahdr_encode, "ember_tone_ahdr_encode");
+  TSYM(ahdr_frame, "ember_tone_ahdr_frame");
+  TSYM(drain_log, "ember_tone_drain_log");
+#undef TSYM
+  if (!tone.abi_version || (tone.abi_version() >> 16) != 1 || !tone.neural_create || !tone.neural_destroy || !tone.neural_encode ||
+      !tone.ahdr_create || !tone.ahdr_destroy || !tone.ahdr_get_config || !tone.ahdr_encode || !tone.ahdr_frame || !tone.drain_log) {
+    memset(&tone, 0, sizeof(tone));
+    dlclose(lib);
+    return;
+  }
+  tone_handle = lib;
+}
+
+/* for ember_neural_unix.m: the loaded library handle (NULL = missing) */
+void *
+ember_tone_lib(void) {
+  pthread_once(&tone_once, tone_load);
+  return tone_handle;
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS
+tone_call(struct unixcall_ember_fg *p) {
+  void *ctx = (void *)(uintptr_t)p->ctx;
+  pthread_once(&tone_once, tone_load);
+  if (!tone.abi_version) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+  switch (p->op) {
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_TONE_NEURAL_CREATE:
+    ctx = tone.neural_create(p->device, (const char *)p->in.ptr, (size_t)p->in_size, 0 /* EMBER_TONE_HOST_DXMT */);
+    p->ctx = (obj_handle_t)(uintptr_t)ctx;
+    p->ret = ctx != NULL;
+    break;
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_TONE_AHDR_CREATE:
+    ctx = tone.ahdr_create(p->device, (const char *)p->in.ptr, (size_t)p->in_size, 0 /* EMBER_TONE_HOST_DXMT */);
+    p->ctx = (obj_handle_t)(uintptr_t)ctx;
+    if (ctx && p->out.ptr) tone.ahdr_get_config(ctx, p->out.ptr);
+    p->ret = ctx != NULL;
+    break;
+  default:
+    if (!ctx) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    switch (p->op) {
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_TONE_NEURAL_ENCODE: p->ret = tone.neural_encode(ctx, p->in.ptr, p->out.ptr); break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_TONE_NEURAL_DESTROY: tone.neural_destroy(ctx); p->ret = 1; return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_TONE_AHDR_ENCODE: p->ret = tone.ahdr_encode(ctx, p->in.ptr, p->out.ptr); break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_TONE_AHDR_FRAME: tone.ahdr_frame(ctx, p->in.ptr, p->out.ptr); p->ret = 1; break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_TONE_AHDR_CONFIG: if (p->out.ptr) tone.ahdr_get_config(ctx, p->out.ptr); p->ret = 1; break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_TONE_AHDR_DESTROY: tone.ahdr_destroy(ctx); p->ret = 1; return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    default: return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    }
+  }
+  if (ctx && p->log.ptr && p->log_cap) p->log_len = tone.drain_log(ctx, (char *)p->log.ptr, (size_t)p->log_cap);
+  return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS spark_call(struct unixcall_ember_fg *p); /* Ember Spark, below */
+
+NTSTATUS
+_EmberFG_call(void *obj) {
+  struct unixcall_ember_fg *p = obj;
+  void *ctx = (void *)(uintptr_t)p->ctx;
+  void *out = p->out.ptr;
+  const void *in = p->in.ptr;
+  pthread_once(&fg_once, fg_load);
+  p->ret = 0;
+  p->log_len = 0;
+  if (p->op >= EMBER_FG_OP_HUD_CREATE && p->op <= EMBER_FG_OP_HUD_DESTROY) return hud_call(p);
+  if (p->op >= EMBER_FG_OP_TONE_NEURAL_CREATE && p->op <= EMBER_FG_OP_TONE_AHDR_DESTROY) return tone_call(p);
+  if (p->op >= EMBER_FG_OP_SPARK_STATE && p->op <= EMBER_FG_OP_SPARK_SLOT) return spark_call(p);
+  if (!fg_version) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+  switch (p->op) {
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_VERSION:
+    p->ret = (int32_t)fg_version;
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_CREATE:
+    ctx = fg.create(p->device, (const char *)in, (size_t)p->in_size);
+    p->ctx = (obj_handle_t)(uintptr_t)ctx;
+    if (ctx && out) fg.get_config(ctx, out);
+    p->ret = ctx != NULL;
+    break;
+  default:
+    if (!ctx) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    switch (p->op) {
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_DESTROY: fg.destroy(ctx); p->ret = 1; return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_CONFIG: if (out) fg.get_config(ctx, out); p->ret = 1; break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_BEGIN: p->ret = fg.begin_frame(ctx, in, out); break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_ENCODE: p->ret = fg.encode(ctx, in, out); break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_RING_ACQUIRE: p->ret = fg.ring_acquire(ctx, in, out); break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_RING_RELEASE: fg.ring_release(ctx, (int32_t)p->arg0, (int32_t)p->arg1); p->ret = 1; break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_RING_IDLE: fg.ring_wait_idle(ctx); p->ret = 1; break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_NOTE_DROP: fg.note_drop(ctx, (uint32_t)p->arg0); p->ret = 1; break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_STATS: if (out) fg.get_stats(ctx, p->arg_i64, out); p->ret = 1; break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_HUD:
+      p->ret = (int32_t)fg.hud_text(ctx, p->arg_i64, p->arg_f64, p->arg1, (char *)out, (size_t)p->out_size);
+      break;
+    case EMBER_FG_OP_DRAIN_LOG: p->ret = 1; break;
+    default: return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    }
+  }
+  if (ctx && p->log.ptr && p->log_cap) p->log_len = fg.drain_log(ctx, (char *)p->log.ptr, (size_t)p->log_cap);
+  return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+/* Ember Kiln (kiln 10-08): libEmberKiln.dylib (EmberCore, separate proprietary library) from the same directory
+ * (EMBER_KILN_LIB overrides). Optional and off unless the Ember app sets EMBER_KILN_DIR (absolute, <Data>/Kiln): then every
+ * pipeline descriptor DXMT builds is noted in <EMBER_KILN_DIR>/<exe>/pipelines.kiln (function names + fixed state only) and the
+ * archive the Ember helper baked from those notes, if it matches this macOS build and GPU, is attached to the descriptor, so a
+ * known pipeline is a lookup instead of a compile. A miss compiles as before. Library or variable missing → nothing happens.
+ * EMBER_KILN_LOG=1 prints pipeline compile times (all pipelines, Kiln on or off) every 5 s while new ones are built. */
+#include <sys/sysctl.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+#include <mach/mach_time.h>
+#include <dispatch/dispatch.h>
+
+static struct {
+  uint32_t (*abi_version)(void);
+  void *(*open)(const char *dir, void *device, int record);
+  void (*close)(void *k);
+  void (*on_render)(void *k, void *desc);
+  void (*on_compute)(void *k, void *desc);
+} kiln;
+static void *kiln_ctx;
+static void *kiln_first_device;
+static pthread_once_t kiln_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+
+/* Windows image name of this process: Wine writes the Windows command line into argv (argv[0] = C:\...\Game.exe).
+ * Same name DXMT uses for its cache folder (dxmt/<exe>/). */
+static int
+kiln_exe_name(char *out, size_t cap) {
+  int mib[3] = {CTL_KERN, KERN_PROCARGS2, getpid()};
+  size_t n = 0;
+  char *b, *p, *e, *a, *s;
+  int argc = 0;
+  out[0] = 0;
+  if (sysctl(mib, 3, NULL, &n, NULL, 0) || n < 8 || !(b = malloc(n))) return 0;
+  if (sysctl(mib, 3, b, &n, NULL, 0)) { free(b); return 0; }
+  memcpy(&argc, b, sizeof(argc));
+  e = b + n;
+  p = b + sizeof(argc);
+  while (p < e && *p) p++;            /* exec path */
+  while (p < e && !*p) p++;           /* padding */
+  a = p;                              /* argv[0] */
+  if (argc > 0 && a < e && *a) {
+    size_t len = strnlen(a, (size_t)(e - a));
+    char tmp[1024];
+    if (len >= sizeof(tmp)) len = sizeof(tmp) - 1;
+    memcpy(tmp, a, len); tmp[len] = 0;
+    s = tmp + strlen(tmp);
+    while (s > tmp && s[-1] != '\\' && s[-1] != '/') s--;
+    if (*s == '"') s++;
+    snprintf(out, cap, "%s", s);
+    if ((s = strchr(out, '"'))) *s = 0;
+  }
+  free(b);
+  return out[0] != 0 && !strchr(out, '/') && strcmp(out, ".") && strcmp(out, "..");
+}
+
+static void
+kiln_atexit(void) {
+  void *k = kiln_ctx;
+  kiln_ctx = NULL;
+  if (k && kiln.close) kiln.close(k);
+}
+
+static void
+kiln_load(void) {
+  char path[4096], exe[256], dir[4096];
+  const char *root = getenv("EMBER_KILN_DIR"), *override = getenv("EMBER_KILN_LIB");
+  void *lib = NULL;
+  Dl_info info;
+  if (!root || root[0] != '/' || !kiln_first_device) return;
+  path[0] = 0;
+  if (override && *override) snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s", override);
+  else if (dladdr((const void *)&kiln_load, &info) && info.dli_fname) {
+    const char *slash = strrchr(info.dli_fname, '/');
+    if (slash) snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%.*s/libEmberKiln.dylib", (int)(slash - info.dli_fname), info.dli_fname);
+  }
+  if (path[0]) lib = dlopen(path, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL);
+  if (!lib) return;
+  *(void **)&kiln.abi_version = dlsym(lib, "ember_kiln_abi_version");
+  *(void **)&kiln.open = dlsym(lib, "ember_kiln_open");
+  *(void **)&kiln.close = dlsym(lib, "ember_kiln_close");
+  *(void **)&kiln.on_render = dlsym(lib, "ember_kiln_on_render_descriptor");
+  *(void **)&kiln.on_compute = dlsym(lib, "ember_kiln_on_compute_descriptor");
+  if (!kiln.abi_version || (kiln.abi_version() >> 16) != 1 || !kiln.open || !kiln.close || !kiln.on_render ||
+      !kiln.on_compute || !kiln_exe_name(exe, sizeof(exe))) {
+    memset(&kiln, 0, sizeof(kiln));
+    dlclose(lib);
+    return;
+  }
+  snprintf(dir, sizeof(dir), "%s/%s", root, exe);
+  kiln_ctx = kiln.open(dir, kiln_first_device, 1);
+  if (kiln_ctx) atexit(kiln_atexit);
+  if (getenv("EMBER_KILN_LOG")) fprintf(stderr, "ember-kiln: %s %s\n", kiln_ctx ? "on" : "open failed", dir);
+}
+
+static void *
+kiln_get(void *device) {
+  if (!device) return NULL;
+  __sync_bool_compare_and_swap(&kiln_first_device, NULL, device);   /* the archive is tied to the first device */
+  pthread_once(&kiln_once, kiln_load);
+  return device == kiln_first_device ? kiln_ctx : NULL;
+}
+
+void
+ember_kiln_render_descriptor(void *device, void *descriptor) {
+  void *k = kiln_get(device);
+  if (k) kiln.on_render(k, descriptor);
+}
+
+void
+ember_kiln_compute_descriptor(void *device, void *descriptor) {
+  void *k = kiln_get(device);
+  if (k) kiln.on_compute(k, descriptor);
+}
+
+/* compile-time log (EMBER_KILN_LOG=1): count and sum of pipeline builds, how many took more than a 60 Hz / 30 Hz frame.
+ * One line at most every 5 s, and always one line 5 s after the last build (so the final totals are in the log). */
+static int kiln_log = -1;
+static pthread_mutex_t kiln_log_mu = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
+static struct { uint64_t n, slow16, slow33, first, last; double total, max; int armed; } kiln_st;
+static mach_timebase_info_data_t kiln_tb;
+
+static double
+kiln_sec(uint64_t d) { return (double)d * kiln_tb.numer / kiln_tb.denom / 1e9; }
+
+static void
+kiln_log_print(void *unused) {
+  (void)unused;
+  pthread_mutex_lock(&kiln_log_mu);
+  kiln_st.armed = 0;
+  fprintf(stderr, "ember-kiln-pso: t=%.1fs n=%llu over16=%llu over33=%llu total=%.0fms max=%.1fms kiln=%d\n",
+          kiln_sec(kiln_st.last - kiln_st.first), (unsigned long long)kiln_st.n, (unsigned long long)kiln_st.slow16,
+          (unsigned long long)kiln_st.slow33, kiln_st.total, kiln_st.max, kiln_ctx != NULL);
+  pthread_mutex_unlock(&kiln_log_mu);
+}
+
+uint64_t
+ember_kiln_time_begin(void) {
+  if (kiln_log < 0) { kiln_log = getenv("EMBER_KILN_LOG") != NULL; mach_timebase_info(&kiln_tb); }
+  return kiln_log ? mach_absolute_time() : 0;
+}
+
+void
+ember_kiln_time_end(uint64_t t0) {
+  uint64_t now;
+  double ms;
+  if (!t0) return;
+  now = mach_absolute_time();
+  ms = kiln_sec(now - t0) * 1e3;
+  pthread_mutex_lock(&kiln_log_mu);
+  if (!kiln_st.first) kiln_st.first = t0;
+  kiln_st.last = now;
+  kiln_st.n++;
+  kiln_st.total += ms;
+  if (ms > kiln_st.max) kiln_st.max = ms;
+  if (ms > 16.7) kiln_st.slow16++;
+  if (ms > 33.3) kiln_st.slow33++;
+  if (!kiln_st.armed) {
+    kiln_st.armed = 1;
+    dispatch_after_f(dispatch_time(DISPATCH_TIME_NOW, 5 * NSEC_PER_SEC), dispatch_get_global_queue(QOS_CLASS_UTILITY, 0),
+                     NULL, kiln_log_print);
+  }
+  pthread_mutex_unlock(&kiln_log_mu);
+}
+
+/* Ember Spark (kiln 10-08): libEmberSpark.dylib (EmberCore, proprietary) from the same directory (EMBER_SPARK_LIB overrides).
+ * Called from EmberFG_call ops 24..28 (ember_fg_call below forwards them here). Off unless EMBER_SPARK=1 or the PE override. */
+static struct {
+  void *(*create)(const void *cfg);
+  void (*set_period)(void *s, double p);
+  void (*enter)(void *s, uint64_t id, double now);
+  double (*exit_)(void *s, uint64_t id, double now);
+  void (*started)(void *s, double now);
+  void (*hint)(void *s, uint32_t kind, uint64_t id, double t);
+  void (*gpu_done)(void *s, uint64_t id, double gs, double ge, double busy);
+  void (*stats)(void *s, void *out);
+} spark;
+static void *spark_ctx;
+static pthread_once_t spark_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+static double spark_period = -1;
+static int spark_log = 0;
+
+static double
+spark_now(void) {
+  if (!kiln_tb.denom) mach_timebase_info(&kiln_tb);
+  return kiln_sec(mach_absolute_time());
+}
+
+static void
+spark_load(void) {
+  char path[4096];
+  const char *override = getenv("EMBER_SPARK_LIB");
+  void *lib = NULL;
+  Dl_info info;
+  path[0] = 0;
+  if (override && *override) snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%s", override);
+  else if (dladdr((const void *)&spark_load, &info) && info.dli_fname) {
+    const char *slash = strrchr(info.dli_fname, '/');
+    if (slash) snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "%.*s/libEmberSpark.dylib", (int)(slash - info.dli_fname), info.dli_fname);
+  }
+  if (path[0]) lib = dlopen(path, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL);
+  if (!lib) return;
+  *(void **)&spark.create = dlsym(lib, "ember_spark_create");
+  *(void **)&spark.set_period = dlsym(lib, "ember_spark_set_period");
+  *(void **)&spark.enter = dlsym(lib, "ember_spark_present_enter");
+  *(void **)&spark.exit_ = dlsym(lib, "ember_spark_present_exit");
+  *(void **)&spark.started = dlsym(lib, "ember_spark_frame_started");
+  *(void **)&spark.hint = dlsym(lib, "ember_spark_hint_slot");
+  *(void **)&spark.gpu_done = dlsym(lib, "ember_spark_gpu_done");
+  *(void **)&spark.stats = dlsym(lib, "ember_spark_get_stats");
+  if (!spark.create || !spark.set_period || !spark.enter || !spark.exit_ || !spark.started || !spark.hint || !spark.gpu_done ||
+      !(spark_ctx = spark.create(NULL))) {
+    memset(&spark, 0, sizeof(spark));
+    dlclose(lib);
+    return;
+  }
+  spark_log = getenv("EMBER_SPARK_LOG") != NULL;
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS
+spark_call(struct unixcall_ember_fg *p) {
+  static int env_on = -1;
+  pthread_once(&spark_once, spark_load);
+  if (!spark_ctx) return STATUS_SUCCESS;   /* ret 0 = no Spark */
+  switch (p->op) {
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_SPARK_STATE:
+    if (env_on < 0) { const char *e = getenv("EMBER_SPARK"); env_on = e && !strcmp(e, "1"); }
+    p->ret = p->arg0 < 0 ? env_on : p->arg0 != 0;
+    break;
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_SPARK_ENTER:
+    if (p->arg_f64 != spark_period) { spark_period = p->arg_f64; spark.set_period(spark_ctx, spark_period > 0 ? spark_period : 0); }
+    spark.enter(spark_ctx, p->arg1, spark_now());
+    p->ret = 1;
+    break;
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_SPARK_EXIT: {
+    double now = spark_now(), s = spark.exit_(spark_ctx, p->arg1, now);
+    if (s > 0) {
+      /* mach_wait_until wakes within ~50 µs; stop 0.3 ms early and spin the rest */
+      uint64_t target = mach_absolute_time() + (uint64_t)(s * 1e9 * kiln_tb.denom / kiln_tb.numer);
+      uint64_t early = (uint64_t)(0.0003 * 1e9 * kiln_tb.denom / kiln_tb.numer);
+      if (s > 0.0005) mach_wait_until(target - early);
+      while (mach_absolute_time() < target) {}
+    }
+    spark.started(spark_ctx, spark_now());
+    p->ret = (int32_t)(s * 1e6);
+    if (spark_log && spark.stats) {
+      static uint64_t last;
+      uint64_t n = mach_absolute_time();
+      if (kiln_sec(n - last) > 5) {
+        struct { uint64_t frames, slept; double avg_sleep_ms, margin_ms, cpu_ms, gpu_ms, bubble_ms; uint32_t mode; double idle; } st;
+        last = n;
+        spark.stats(spark_ctx, &st);
+        fprintf(stderr, "ember-spark: frames=%llu held=%llu sleep=%.2fms margin=%.2fms cpu=%.2fms gpu=%.2fms bubble=%.2fms mode=%u idle=%.3f period=%.2fms\n",
+                (unsigned long long)st.frames, (unsigned long long)st.slept, st.avg_sleep_ms, st.margin_ms, st.cpu_ms, st.gpu_ms,
+                st.bubble_ms, st.mode, st.idle, spark_period * 1e3);
+      }
+    }
+    break;
+  }
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_SPARK_GPU:
+    spark.gpu_done(spark_ctx, p->arg1, (double)p->arg_i64 * 1e-9, (double)p->arg0 * 1e-9, p->arg_f64);
+    p->ret = 1;
+    break;
+  case EMBER_FG_OP_SPARK_SLOT:
+    spark.hint(spark_ctx, (uint32_t)p->arg0, p->arg1, spark_now() + p->arg_f64);
+    p->ret = 1;
+    break;
+  }
+  return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
diff --git a/src/winemetal/unix/ember_neural_unix.m b/src/winemetal/unix/ember_neural_unix.m
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6a64e53
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/winemetal/unix/ember_neural_unix.m
@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@
+/*
+ * Ember Tone: old winemetal unix calls 146~152 (EmberNeural_* in ember_neural_thunks.c), kept for DXMT builds that still drive
+ * the CoreML worker themselves (older d3d12.dll). The worker now lives in libEmberTone.dylib (EmberCore, separate proprietary
+ * library, loaded by ember_fg_unix.c); these entry points only forward to it. Without the library open() fails and those
+ * builds fall back to their baseline pass. New DXMT builds use EmberFG_call ops EMBER_FG_OP_TONE_* instead.
+ * Integration (unchanged): winemetal_unix.c appends &_EmberNeural_open … &_EmberNeural_stats (146~152) to both call tables.
+ *
+ * This library is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU Lesser
+ * General Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation; either version 2.1 of the License, or
+ * (at your option) any later version.
+ */
+#include <dlfcn.h>
+#include <pthread.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+#define WINEMETAL_API
+#include "../winemetal_thunks.h"
+#include "../ember_neural_thunks.h"
+
+typedef int NTSTATUS;            /* same definition as winemetal_unix.c */
+#define STATUS_SUCCESS 0
+
+void *ember_tone_lib(void);      /* ember_fg_unix.c */
+
+/* EmberCore/tone/include/ember_tone.h: ember_tone_ane_stats */
+struct tone_ane_stats {
+    uint64_t done, skipped, failed;
+    double ms_ema, ms_last, ms_max, open_ms;
+    int32_t layout, width, height;
+    char units[16];
+    char path[512];
+};
+
+static struct {
+    void *(*open)(uint64_t device, const char *spec, int want_w, int want_h, const char *units, int log);
+    void (*close)(void *a);
+    void (*desc)(void *a, int32_t *w, int32_t *h, int32_t *layout, float norm[4]);
+    int (*begin)(void *a, uint64_t *input_texture);
+    void (*submit)(void *a, uint64_t command_buffer, int slot);
+    void (*cancel)(void *a, int slot);
+    int (*latest)(void *a, uint64_t *lo_in, uint64_t *lo_out, uint64_t *seq, int32_t *age);
+    void (*stats)(void *a, struct tone_ane_stats *s);
+} ane;
+static pthread_once_t ane_once = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+
+static void
+ane_load(void) {
+    void *lib = ember_tone_lib();
+    if (!lib) return;
+    *(void **)&ane.open = dlsym(lib, "ember_tone_ane_open");
+    *(void **)&ane.close = dlsym(lib, "ember_tone_ane_close");
+    *(void **)&ane.desc = dlsym(lib, "ember_tone_ane_desc");
+    *(void **)&ane.begin = dlsym(lib, "ember_tone_ane_begin");
+    *(void **)&ane.submit = dlsym(lib, "ember_tone_ane_submit");
+    *(void **)&ane.cancel = dlsym(lib, "ember_tone_ane_cancel");
+    *(void **)&ane.latest = dlsym(lib, "ember_tone_ane_latest");
+    *(void **)&ane.stats = dlsym(lib, "ember_tone_ane_get_stats");
+    if (!ane.open || !ane.close || !ane.desc || !ane.begin || !ane.submit || !ane.cancel || !ane.latest || !ane.stats)
+        memset(&ane, 0, sizeof(ane));
+}
+
+static int
+ane_ok(void) {
+    pthread_once(&ane_once, ane_load);
+    return ane.open != NULL;
+}
+
+NTSTATUS _EmberNeural_open(void *obj)
+{
+    struct unixcall_ember_neural_open *p = obj;
+    const char *units = p->units.ptr ? (const char *)p->units.ptr : "";
+    struct ember_neural_ane_desc *desc = p->desc.ptr;
+    void *a = ane_ok() ? ane.open(p->device, (const char *)p->spec.ptr, (int)p->want_w, (int)p->want_h, *units ? units : NULL,
+                                  (int)p->log) : NULL;
+    p->ret = (obj_handle_t)(uintptr_t)a;
+    if (a && desc)
+    {
+        int32_t w = 0, h = 0, layout = 0;
+        float norm[4] = {1, 0, 1, 0};
+        ane.desc(a, &w, &h, &layout, norm);
+        desc->width = (uint32_t)w;
+        desc->height = (uint32_t)h;
+        desc->layout = (uint32_t)layout;
+        desc->in_scale = norm[0]; desc->in_bias = norm[1]; desc->out_scale = norm[2]; desc->out_bias = norm[3];
+    }
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+NTSTATUS _EmberNeural_close(void *obj)
+{
+    struct unixcall_generic_obj_noret *p = obj;
+    if (ane_ok()) ane.close((void *)(uintptr_t)p->handle);
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+NTSTATUS _EmberNeural_begin(void *obj)
+{
+    struct unixcall_ember_neural_begin *p = obj;
+    uint64_t t = 0;
+    p->ret_slot = ane_ok() && p->ctx ? ane.begin((void *)(uintptr_t)p->ctx, &t) : -1;
+    p->ret_texture = (obj_handle_t)t;   /* owned by the worker (the slot keeps it); the PE side borrows it */
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+NTSTATUS _EmberNeural_submit(void *obj)
+{
+    struct unixcall_ember_neural_submit *p = obj;
+    if (ane_ok() && p->ctx) ane.submit((void *)(uintptr_t)p->ctx, (uint64_t)p->cmdbuf, p->slot);
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+NTSTATUS _EmberNeural_cancel(void *obj)
+{
+    struct unixcall_ember_neural_submit *p = obj;
+    if (ane_ok() && p->ctx) ane.cancel((void *)(uintptr_t)p->ctx, p->slot);
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+NTSTATUS _EmberNeural_latest(void *obj)
+{
+    struct unixcall_ember_neural_latest *p = obj;
+    uint64_t in = 0, out = 0, seq = 0;
+    int32_t age = 0;
+    p->ret_ok = ane_ok() && p->ctx ? ane.latest((void *)(uintptr_t)p->ctx, &in, &out, &seq, &age) : 0;
+    p->ret_in = (obj_handle_t)in;
+    p->ret_out = (obj_handle_t)out;
+    p->ret_seq = seq;
+    p->ret_age = age;
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+NTSTATUS _EmberNeural_stats(void *obj)
+{
+    struct unixcall_ember_neural_stats *p = obj;
+    struct tone_ane_stats s;
+    memset(&s, 0, sizeof(s));
+    if (ane_ok() && p->ctx) ane.stats((void *)(uintptr_t)p->ctx, &s);
+    p->done = s.done; p->skipped = s.skipped; p->failed = s.failed;
+    p->ms_ema = s.ms_ema; p->ms_max = s.ms_max; p->open_ms = s.open_ms;
+    return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+}
